  "result": "Quiz 0002 is ready, with six questions on O4 (workflows versus agents, and who owns the control flow). The files are `quizzes/0002.json` and `keys/0002.json`.\n\nThe questions use the makerspace assistant as the running example:\n- **Definition:** what separates a workflow from an agent (one multiple-choice question).\n- **Classification:** whether a fixed search-then-answer pipeline is a workflow or an agent (one multiple-choice question).\n- **Fixed workflow vs. agent:** whether the booking steps should be a fixed workflow, and which kind of request most justifies letting the model choose its steps (one short answer and one multiple-choice).\n- **Budget:** how much more an agent costs than a workflow over 500 requests (one numeric question).\n- **Routing:** who owns the control flow when a model labels the request and code then picks the pipeline (one short answer).\n\nNo lesson on O4 exists yet, so the quiz is ahead of the lessons. I wrote it from my own knowledge of the workflow/agent distinction, as Anthropic's \"Building effective agents\" frames it. I didn't search the web or check that source this session. The multiple-choice questions use no misconception ids, because I couldn't see definitions for the existing ones (M1 to M6).\n\nWould you like a short lesson on O4 before you take it?",
